# clamber-scenario v1
id: exit-walk-out
summary: After the entrance, walk left towards an exit, turn right just inside its reach and let go, so the exit takes over a lead facing right; then press Jump, Action and Right during the walk-out, which change nothing.
requires: the first level begun from the level map, with its entrance at the start point (behavior/level-start.md); flat floor 185 px below the start point, from 88 px to 360 px right of it, with nothing above it up to the start point's height from 88 px to 136 px right of it; at the floor's left end, 88 px right of the start point, a vertical step up (behavior/steep-faces.md), with the ground at least 64 px higher than the floor from 56 px to 88 px right of the start point; an exit (behavior/exits.md) leading left at 60 px right of the start point and 185 px below it, at the floor's height inside that higher ground; no walls or other ground along the throw's path; no entities other than the entrance and the exit within 120 px of the player at any time
start: the level's first frame (behavior/level-start.md), one character, nothing held before frame 0
frames: 199

[inputs]
120-143  L
144-146  R
158-163  J
170-185  A
175-190  R

[metrics]
final_x          tol 1
final_y          tol 0.5
curve x,y,vx from land for 92 tol 0.25
